    ("The digital learning platform deployed under Mission Karmayogi for continuous competency development of civil servants is:", "iGOT Karmayogi (Integrated Government Online Training)", ["DIKSHA Portal", "SWAYAM Prabha", "Coursera India"], "iGOT provides role-based curated courses, assessments, and continuous professional learning modules for public servants."),
    ("Under the 'National Green Hydrogen Mission', the SIGHT programme stands for:", "Strategic Interventions for Green Hydrogen Transition (subsidizing electrolyzer manufacturing and hydrogen production)", ["Satellite Imagery for Green Highland Terrain", "Strategic Infrastructure for Global Highway Transit", "Solar Installation for Governmental Hospital Trusts"], "SIGHT allocates Rs 17,490 crore for domestic electrolyser manufacturing and domestic green hydrogen production."),
    ("In the 'Aspirational Districts Programme' (ADP), what are the five core thematic sectors and their respective weightages?", "Health & Nutrition (30%), Education (30%), Agriculture & Water (20%), Financial Inclusion & Skill (10%), Infrastructure (10%)", ["Military (50%), Police (30%), Prisons (20%)", "Mining (40%), Heavy Industry (40%), Aviation (20%)", "Real Estate (60%), Banking (30%), Tourism (10%)"], "ADP metrics emphasize human development (health, education, nutrition) as driving 60% of district ranking scores."),
    ("The 'Aspirational Blocks Programme' (ABP) launched in 2023 scales the ADP framework down to:", "500 lagging administrative development blocks across 329 districts", ["All 6,000 blocks in India simultaneously", "Only urban municipal corporation wards", "Exclusively cantonment board areas"], "ABP targets deep intra-district inequalities, tracking progress on key performance indicators on delta rankings."),
    ("In the 'Production Linked Incentive' (PLI) scheme for Large Scale Electronics, what is the required baseline criteria for firms?", "Incremental investment and incremental production thresholds over a four to six-year commitment period", ["Hiring only workers with PhD qualifications", "Exporting 100% of manufactured goods to Antarctica", "Using zero electricity in factory production"], "Firms receive incentive payouts only upon verifying audited capital investment and incremental sales thresholds."),
    ("Under the 'PM Vishwakarma Scheme', the financial collateral-free credit support is provided at which subsidized interest rate?", "Subsidized concessional interest rate of 5% (with 8% interest subvention paid by MoMSME)", ["Zero interest with complete principal waiver", "Market commercial rate of 18%", "Compounded monthly interest of 24%"], "Eligible artisans receive enterprise loans of Rs 1 lakh (first tranche) and Rs 2 lakh (second tranche) at 5% interest."),
    ("Under the 'PM Surya Ghar: Muft Bijli Yojana', what central financial assistance (subsidy) is provided for a 2 kW rooftop solar system?", "Rs 60,000 (Rs 30,000 per kW up to 2 kW, and Rs 18,000 for the 3rd kW up to max Rs 78,000)", ["Rs 10,000 total subsidy", "100% of the cost up to Rs 5 lakh", "Rs 5,000 coupon for electric bulbs"], "The scheme subsidizes up to Rs 78,000 for 3 kW systems, making clean rooftop solar affordable for middle-class homes."),
    ("The 'Jal Jeevan Mission' mandates that post-construction operation and maintenance of village water infrastructure is handed to:", "Village Water and Sanitation Committees (VWSC) / Pani Samitis under the Gram Panchayat", ["Private foreign water multinational corporations", "The Central Ground Water Board engineers exclusively", "The state police department"], "Pani Samitis (with at least 50% women members) prepare Village Action Plans and manage daily water supply."),
    ("The 'PM-PRANAM' scheme finances alternative fertilizer technology incentives by using which funding mechanism?", "50% of the fiscal subsidy savings generated by a State through reduction in chemical fertilizer consumption", ["A new national education cess levied on income tax", "Commercial loans borrowed from international sovereign banks", "Confiscating corporate agricultural warehouse assets"], "States that reduce conventional urea consumption receive 50% of the central fertilizer subsidy savings as grant funds."),
    ("Under the 'National Clean Air Programme' (NCAP), city funding from the 15th Finance Commission Air Quality Grant is contingent upon:", "Achieving targeted percentage reductions in PM concentrations and expanding ambient air monitoring networks", ["Banning all motorized personal vehicles immediately", "Planting 10 million fruit trees inside public parks", "Relocating all factories outside state borders"], "Performance-based grants reward municipal corporations that achieve measurable improvements in air quality indices."),
    ("In the 'SVAMITVA' drone mapping methodology, what technical base stations are established to ensure centimeter-level accuracy?", "CORS (Continuously Operating Reference Stations) network established by Survey of India", ["Standard mobile telephone 4G cellular towers", "Commercial FM radio broadcasting transmitters", "Local village police wireless antennas"], "CORS networks provide real-time kinematic positioning down to 5 centimeters for legal property demarcation."),
    ("The 'Digital India Bhashini' (National Language Translation Mission) initiative leverages AI and NLP to:", "Enable voice-based citizen access to public digital services in 22 official Indian scheduled languages", ["Teach computer programming in Latin only", "Translate all legal acts into classical Sanskrit exclusively", "Ban all foreign internet websites nationwide"], "Bhashini breaks language barriers, allowing unlettered and non-English speaking citizens to access e-governance via voice."),
    ("The 'Stand-Up India' scheme was extended up to 2025 with which major policy modification in the margin money requirement?", "Margin money requirement for loans was reduced from up to 25% down to up to 15%", ["Margin money was increased to 50%", "Loans were restricted exclusively to software startups", "Borrowers were required to provide gold collateral"], "Lowering the margin money requirement to 15% expanded access for first-time SC/ST and women entrepreneurs."),
    ("Under the 'PM Matsya Sampada Yojana' (PMMSY), what innovative technology is promoted to revolutionize inland fish production?", "Recirculatory Aquaculture Systems (RAS) and Biofloc technology for high-density eco-friendly farming", ["Bottom-trawling that scours riverbeds", "Adding toxic industrial chemicals to reservoirs", "Draining natural freshwater lakes for housing"], "Biofloc and RAS recycle water, produce microbial protein feed, and increase fish yields in limited land space."),
    ("The 'National Apprenticeship Promotion Scheme' (NAPS) incentivizes employers to engage apprentices by:", "Reimbursing 25% of prescribed stipend up to Rs 1,500 per month per apprentice directly to employers", ["Paying 100% of all company executive salaries", "Exempting participating corporations from all environmental laws", "Granting monopoly government procurement contracts"], "NAPS bridges the skill gap by co-funding practical workplace training across manufacturing and services."),
    ("Under the 'PM Mega Integrated Textile Regions and Apparel' (PM MITRA) scheme, parks are developed with plug-and-play facilities under:", "Public-Private Partnership (PPP) model managed by a Special Purpose Vehicle (SPV) owned by Central and State Govts", ["Direct ownership by foreign commercial fashion brands", "Complete administration by municipal village panchayats", "Informal cooperative trusts without registration"], "PM MITRA creates world-class integrated textile value chains (fiber to fashion) across 7 mega parks."),
    ("The 'Deen Dayal Upadhyaya Grameen Kaushalya Yojana' (DDU-GKY) under MoRD mandates which post-training outcome benchmark?", "Guaranteed placement of at least 70% of trained rural youth with regular monthly salaries above minimum wage", ["Issuing participation paper certificates without job assistance", "Mandatory relocation of youth to foreign nations", "Offering unpaid voluntary internships only"], "DDU-GKY is a placement-linked skill scheme targeted at poor rural youth to ensure sustainable wage employment."),
    ("Under the 'PM Gati Shakti' master plan, what is the role of the 'Network Planning Group' (NPG)?", "Evaluating all infrastructure connectivity proposals above Rs 500 crore to ensure multimodal integration and eliminate duplication", ["Auditing annual income tax returns of corporate builders", "Approving commercial airline ticket pricing tariffs", "Designing architectural floor plans for government staff quarters"], "NPG comprises planning heads from Railways, MoRTH, Shipping, Telecom, and Power to review project coherence."),
    ("The 'Mission Vatsalya' implemented by the Ministry of Women and Child Development focuses on:", "Child protection services, juvenile justice, foster care, and institutional rehabilitation of children in distress", ["Distributing free baby food to private hospitals", "Managing state adoption agencies for foreign tourists", "Operating commercial children's amusement parks"], "Mission Vatsalya establishes child care institutions, specialized adoption agencies, and child welfare committees."),
    ("The 'PM-JAY' anti-fraud architecture deploys which technology mechanism to detect ghost beneficiaries and hospital fraud?", "Artificial Intelligence, Machine Learning fraud analytics algorithms, and National Anti-Fraud Unit (NAFU) audits", ["Relying exclusively on handwritten paper complaint boxes", "Ignoring all over-billing reports from private clinics", "Banning all private hospital empanelments entirely"], "NAFU monitors outlier claim spikes, triggers field audits, and de-empanels hospitals committing phantom surgeries."),
    ("The 'Bharat Interface for Money' (BHIM) and UPI ecosystem developed by NPCI is governed as a:", "Digital Public Good (DPG) and public digital infrastructure operating on interoperable open protocols", ["Proprietary closed software monopolized by a private bank", "Commercial credit card network charging 3% swipe fees", "Classified military surveillance telecommunications system"], "UPI provides open, interoperable, real-time mobile payment rails enabling innovation and universal financial access."),
    ("Under the 'National Rural Drinking Water Quality Monitoring and Surveillance Programme', testing at village level is conducted via:", "Field Test Kits (FTKs) deployed by trained village women (Jal Sahiyas) for basic chemical and bacteriological parameters", ["Shipping all water samples to overseas foreign laboratories", "Drinking untreated raw water to test toxicity by human reaction", "Using satellite cameras to measure chemical dissolved ions"], "Women are trained to use portable FTKs to test pH, turbidity, chlorine, nitrate, and pathogens in village water.")
